# Folkprotocol Site Draft v0
#
# Eleventh experimental slice. It converts a closed, triaged tone draft into a
# collection-compatible candidate without overwriting live site content.

Expect slug
Default work_dir: /home/patrick/projects/folkprotocol

Work in {work_dir}

Codex: """Prepare an editorial site candidate from the completed Folkprotocol
run at research/source-maps/{slug}/.

Required research inputs are 00-commission.md, 01-editorial-direction.md,
80-practice-assessment.md,
120-tone-draft.md,
133-audit-triage.md, 134-citation-recheck.md, 135-content-recheck.md,
136-tone-repair-check.md, and 137-audit-closure.md. Verify every completion
marker and require the exact final line `AUDIT CLOSURE COMPLETE — READY`. If
closure requires repair, stop without writing. Verify that 137 is current by
recomputing its documented digest from research/source-maps/{slug}/ with
exactly `sha256sum 120-tone-draft.md 133-audit-triage.md
134-citation-recheck.md 135-content-recheck.md 136-tone-repair-check.md |
sha256sum`; stop on any mismatch.

Also read src/content/config.ts and docs/citations.md. Derive the topic filename
by removing a terminal version suffix such as `-v1` from {slug}; for
`hangover-v1`, this yields `hangover`. Read only
`src/content/protocols/<derived-topic>.md` to learn the current collection frontmatter,
citation conventions, and relevant internal links. Stop if the file is absent
or its topic does not match 00-commission.md. Do not treat its prose or
bibliography as authority.

From research/source-maps/{slug}/ compute the research input digest with
exactly `sha256sum 00-commission.md 01-editorial-direction.md 80-practice-assessment.md
120-tone-draft.md 133-audit-triage.md
134-citation-recheck.md 135-content-recheck.md 136-tone-repair-check.md
137-audit-closure.md | sha256sum`.
Write research/source-maps/{slug}/140-site-draft.md with that digest as
inputDigest and `draft: true` in YAML frontmatter. If a complete site draft
records the same digest, leave it unchanged.

Read only the named files and the existing output. Do no web research, do not
delegate or start another agent workflow, and do not edit anything under
src/content/. Write only 140-site-draft.md.

Produce frontmatter accepted by the protocols collection:

- `title`
- a concrete one-sentence `summary`
- `researchDepth`, using one allowed enum from src/content/config.ts
- a short `symptoms` list grounded in the page
- only existing relevant protocol collection IDs. Inspect the IDs produced by
  the current collection and route rather than inferring them from a preferred
  URL style. With the present loader, `nausea.md` produces
  `/protocols/nausea.md/`; neither `nausea` nor `protocols/nausea` is the
  correct ID. The old page may suggest relevance but is not authority for a
  malformed ID
- `draft: true`
- `inputDigest`

Below frontmatter, make an editorial candidate from the verified material. You
may cut, condense, and reorder prose, but may not add factual claims or change a
claim's force. Use the commission and its accounting in 80 to decide what the
page is principally about. A direction selected for research does not earn
equal space merely because a dossier exists.

Prefer a short explanatory structure organized around the distinct processes,
symptom paths, or decision points that actually help the reader. Attach
practices to the path and moment they address. Do not produce a parade of
coequal remedy sections, an inventory of everything found, or a concluding
miscellany that restores material cut earlier. Preserve unresolved commissioner
leads when they define the next useful questions, clearly as first-person leads
rather than general findings.

Keep prose above `## References` between 1,200 and 2,800 words unless the
verified material genuinely requires less. Include only references cited in
that prose. Renumber citations and references sequentially. Render references
as public bibliography entries: retain identity, title, date, stable URL, and
material access qualifications; remove research workflow, ownership, and
`contributed`/`taken from it` annotations. Verify mechanically that prose
citations and reference numbers are identical sets with no gaps.

Replace the research completion marker with `SITE DRAFT COMPLETE — N
references`. Do not add a recommendation tier, default stack, quantified-self
routine, medical disclaimer, publication claim, or new factual content. This
is a draft for editorial approval, not a live publish.""" model=gpt-5.6-sol, timeout=1200
